From 2ac1a29f2d8d87f0206830683c5522e8872858b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Kuderski <jakub@nod-labs.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:35:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [rocr][clr] Load gfx1250 code objects with fixed-on XNACK

LLVM main emits XNACK ON for gfx1250, gfx1250-strict, and gfx12-5-generic.
ROCr converts that flag into an unregistered :xnack+ ISA name and rejects
the code object. HIP also rejects the same spelling returned by older
COMGR versions before reaching the HSA loader.

Use the bare processor names for permanently enabled XNACK in ROCr and
normalize COMGR's legacy spelling in CLR. Preserve compatibility with
UNSUPPORTED and ANY encodings while rejecting explicit OFF code objects.

Add opt-in LLVM smoke tests through HIP and direct HSA for the three
targets plus gfx90a and gfx950. Compare direct and assembly-path ELF flags,
check compatible dispatch results, and cover incompatible feature modes.
Use separate metadata controls without modifying compiler-produced objects.

Rebuilt ROCr, CLR, and RocJITsu. All 10 compiler compatibility tests and
three existing HSA/HIP integration tests pass, with 128 checked results
per smoke dispatch and no RocJITsu implementation changes.

(cherry picked from commit 056ef984360b80bef95c66abff9d0a1fb0a5ef73)
